Ghost,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/Ghost/pull/4,Missing dependency in useEffect causes stale clamp detection,"The CommentContent component's useEffect hook has an empty dependency array, but it uses item.html to determine if content should be clamped. When a comment's HTML content changes (e.g., after an edit or when new data is loaded), the clamp detection won't re-run. This means the 'Show more' button may appear when it shouldn't or disappear when it should still be visible, creating a poor user experience. The dependency array should include item.html to ensure the clamp detection re-runs whenever the content changes.",apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx,92.0,104.0,"    useEffect(() => {
        const checkIfClamped = () => {
            if (contentRef.current) {
                // Check if the content is clamped by comparing scrollHeight with clientHeight
                setIsClamped(contentRef.current.scrollHeight > contentRef.current.clientHeight);
            }
        };

        checkIfClamped();
        // Recheck on window resize
        window.addEventListener('resize', checkIfClamped);
        return () => window.removeEventListener('resize', checkIfClamped);
    }, []);",
Ghost,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/Ghost/pull/4,Filter button becomes non-functional when onAddFilter is undefined,"The conditional check for rendering the post title button was changed from `item.post?.id && item.post?.title && onAddFilter` to `item.post?.id && item.post?.title`, removing the onAddFilter null check. However, the button's onClick handler still calls onAddFilter('post', item.post!.id). Since onAddFilter is now a required prop in the TypeScript signature but the runtime check was removed, if onAddFilter is ever undefined or null at runtime, clicking the post title button will throw an error and crash the component. The original three-part condition was protecting against this scenario.",apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx,236.0,248.0,"                                                {item.post?.id && item.post?.title ? (
                                                    <Button
                                                        className=""block h-auto truncate p-0 font-medium  text-primary hover:opacity-70""
                                                        variant=""link""
                                                        onClick={() => onAddFilter('post', item.post!.id)}
                                                    >
                                                        {item.post.title}
                                                    </Button>
                                                ) : (
                                                    <span className=""text-muted-foreground"">
                                                    Unknown post
                                                    </span>
                                                )}",
Ghost,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/Ghost/pull/4,Inconsistent conditional rendering pattern for feature image,"The feature image rendering logic was changed from a ternary expression with explicit null return (`condition ? <img /> : null`) to a logical AND operator (`condition && <img />`). While functionally similar in most cases, this creates an inconsistency: when item.post?.feature_image is falsy (like an empty string ''), the logical AND will render the falsy value (empty string) instead of rendering nothing. This could lead to unexpected DOM nodes or React warnings. The original ternary with explicit null was more defensive and clearer about the intent to render nothing when the condition is false.",apps/posts/src/views/comments/components/comments-list.tsx,350.0,358.0,"                                <TableCell className=""col-start-2 col-end-2 row-start-2 row-end-3 p-0 text-right align-top md:col-start-3 md:col-end-3 lg:table-cell lg:p-4"">
                                    {item.post?.feature_image && (
                                        <img
                                            alt={item.post.title || 'Post feature image'}
                                            className=""hidden aspect-video w-32 rounded object-cover lg:block""
                                            src={item.post.feature_image}
                                        />
                                    )}
                                </TableCell>",
Ghost,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/Ghost/pull/4,Delete comment functionality completely removed from UI,"The PR removes the dropdown menu item that allowed users to delete comments, making the delete functionality completely inaccessible through the UI. While all the backend infrastructure remains intact (AlertDialog component, confirmDelete function, deleteComment mutation, commentToDelete state), there is no button or menu item that calls setCommentToDelete to trigger the deletion flow. This is a critical functional regression that removes an essential moderation capability for administrators. Users can no longer delete comments through the interface, even though the API endpoint and confirmation dialog are still present in the code.",,,,"<DropdownMenu>
    <DropdownMenuTrigger asChild>
        <Button className=""relative z-10 ml-1"" size=""sm"" variant=""ghost"">
            <LucideIcon.Ellipsis />
        </Button>
    </DropdownMenuTrigger>
    <DropdownMenuContent align=""start"">
        {item.post?.url && (
            <DropdownMenuItem asChild>
                <a href={item.post.url} rel=""noopener noreferrer"" target=""_blank"">
                    <LucideIcon.ExternalLink className=""mr-2 size-4"" />
                    View post
                </a>
            </DropdownMenuItem>
        )}
        {item.member?.id && (
            <DropdownMenuItem asChild>
                <a href={`#/members/${item.member.id}`}>
                    <LucideIcon.User className=""mr-2 size-4"" />
                    View member
                </a>
            </DropdownMenuItem>
        )}
    </DropdownMenuContent>
</DropdownMenu>",
