    setSuccess(true);
} else {",
Ghost,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/Ghost/pull/5,Email trimming creates validation and display inconsistency,"The form now trims the email on submission but validates and displays the untrimmed version. If a user enters ' user@example.com ' (with spaces), the validator checks the untrimmed email which passes validation (spaces don't invalidate the regex), but the API receives 'user@example.com' (trimmed). This creates confusion where the displayed email in the UI doesn't match what was actually submitted, and could cause issues if the user needs to verify what they signed up with. The trim should either be applied before validation and reflected in the display, or not applied at all.",apps/signup-form/src/components/pages/form-view.tsx,54.0,56.0,"const submitHandler: FormEventHandler<HTMLFormElement> = (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    onSubmit({email: email.trim()});
};",
