Ghost,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/Ghost/pull/7,Incorrect require paths for email service dependencies causing initialization failure,"The require statements reference 'email-event-storage' and 'email-event-processor' (kebab-case) but these files remain as 'EmailEventStorage.js' and 'EmailEventProcessor.js' (PascalCase) and were not renamed in this PR. When the email analytics service initializes, Node.js will fail to resolve these module paths and throw MODULE_NOT_FOUND errors. This breaks the entire email analytics system, preventing the tracking of email opens, clicks, bounces, and other email engagement metrics. The correct paths should be '../email-service/EmailEventStorage' and '../email-service/EmailEventProcessor' to match the actual unrenamed files.",ghost/core/core/server/services/email-analytics/email-analytics-service-wrapper.js,11.0,13.0,"const EmailAnalyticsService = require('./email-analytics-service');
