Ghost,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/Ghost/pull/11,Race condition: search input cleared synchronously causes visual glitch,"The handleClose function was modified to clear the search input synchronously using setSearchInput('') instead of the debounced setTimeout(() => setSearchInput(''), 200). This creates a race condition where the search input is cleared while the popover closing animation is still running, causing a visible flash where the filtered results disappear before the popover closes. The original implementation used a 200ms delay to allow the popover animation to complete before clearing the search state, preventing visual artifacts. This bug affects user experience by showing jarring UI state changes during the transition.",apps/shade/src/components/ui/filters.tsx,1049.0,1053.0,"    const handleClose = () => {
        setOpen(false);
        setSearchInput('');
        onClose?.();
    };",
Ghost,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/Ghost/pull/11,Missing handleClose call in single-select mode prevents search input cleanup,"In the unselected options section for single-select mode, the code calls setOpen(false) but fails to call handleClose(), unlike the multiselect path which properly calls handleClose() when autoCloseOnSelect is enabled. This means when a user selects a single option, the popover closes but the search input state is never cleared, causing the next time the popover opens to show stale search results and filtered options from the previous interaction. The handleClose() function is responsible for clearing the search input and triggering the onClose callback, both of which are now skipped in single-select scenarios.",apps/shade/src/components/ui/filters.tsx,1275.0,1278.0,"                                                } else {
                                                    onChange([option.value] as T[]);
                                                    setOpen(false);
                                                }",
Ghost,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/Ghost/pull/11,Memory leak: temporary selected values not cleared on filter popover close,"The onClose handler in the SelectOptionsPopover component was modified to remove the setTempSelectedValues([]) cleanup call. This causes a memory leak where tempSelectedValues state persists after the popover closes. When a user opens the add filter popover, selects a field that supports options, starts selecting values, then closes the popover without confirming, those temporary values remain in state. If the user then opens a different field's options, they may see incorrect pre-selected values carried over from the previous interaction. The original PR correctly added this cleanup in line 2102 to ensure temporary state is cleared, but this bug removes it causing state pollution across different filter field selections.",apps/shade/src/components/ui/filters.tsx,2098.0,2101.0,"                                    onClose={() => {
                                        setAddFilterOpen(false);
                                        setSelectedFieldKeyForOptions(null);
                                    }}",
Ghost,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/Ghost/pull/11,autoCloseOnSelect fails to close popover in non-inline multiselect mode,"The autoCloseOnSelect feature was implemented inconsistently across inline and non-inline modes. In non-inline Popover mode (line 1135-1137), when a multiselect option is selected with autoCloseOnSelect enabled, the code only calls onClose?.() without calling setOpen(false). Since SelectOptionsPopover can be instantiated without an onClose prop (line 1598), the optional chaining results in a no-op, leaving the popover open despite user selection. This breaks the intended UX where the dropdown should close immediately after selection when autoCloseOnSelect is configured. The inline mode implementation (line 1272-1273) correctly calls handleClose() which performs both operations.",,,,"// Auto-close if configured
if (field.autoCloseOnSelect) {
    onClose?.();
}
// For multiselect, don't close the popover to allow multiple selections",
Ghost,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/Ghost/pull/11,Double-quoted string literal used in JSX attribute,Rule requires single quotes for string literals. The updated JSX uses a double-quoted string for the className attribute in the modified line.,apps/shade/src/components/ui/filters.tsx,943.0,943.0,"<div className=""flex items-center self-stretch border border-r-[0px] px-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground"">",Code Must Use Single Quotes for Strings
Ghost,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/Ghost/pull/12,Documentation references npm instead of yarn,"The rule requires all package management commands to use yarn, but the code documentation references npm commands for installing and running Tinybird tools",ghost/core/core/server/services/tinybird/TinybirdService.js,61.0,67.0,"/**
 * Service for managing Tinybird JWT tokens and authentication
