                            # Serialize dict to JSON string
                            json_str = json.dumps(subscription_plan)
                            pipe.setex(redis_key, cls._PLAN_CACHE_TTL, json_str)
                        pipe.execute()",
dify,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/dify/pull/10,Type contract violation in get_plan_bulk return value,"In the get_plan_bulk method, when subscription plan validation fails for a tenant, the code sets `results[tenant_id] = None` instead of skipping that tenant with `continue`. This violates the method's return type contract of `dict[str, SubscriptionPlan]` by inserting None values. Downstream consumers expecting valid SubscriptionPlan objects will encounter AttributeError or TypeError when attempting to access plan fields like `subscription_plan['plan']` or `subscription_plan['expiration_date']`. This bug can cascade through the caching layer in get_plan_bulk_with_cache, potentially storing None values in Redis.",api/services/billing_service.py,284.0,292.0,"                for tenant_id, plan in data.items():
                    try:
                        subscription_plan = subscription_adapter.validate_python(plan)
                        results[tenant_id] = subscription_plan
                    except Exception:
                        logger.exception(
                            ""get_plan_bulk: failed to validate subscription plan for tenant(%s)"", tenant_id
                        )
                        results[tenant_id] = None",
dify,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/dify/pull/10,Incorrect cache count in observability logging,"In the get_plan_bulk_with_cache method, the logging statement reports `len(bulk_plans)` as the number of cached items instead of `len(plans_to_cache)`. This creates misleading observability metrics. When some tenant plans fail validation or are filtered out, bulk_plans will contain more entries than plans_to_cache, causing the log to report an inflated count of successfully cached items. This makes it difficult to diagnose caching issues and can mask problems where fewer plans are actually cached than expected.",api/services/billing_service.py,380.0,383.0,"                        logger.info(
                            ""get_plan_bulk_with_cache: cached %s new tenant plans to Redis"",
                            len(bulk_plans),
                        )",
dify,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/dify/pull/10,Raising generic Exception instead of domain-specific exception,"New code raises a generic `Exception` from a service method. Per the rule, backend services should raise domain-specific exceptions (e.g., from `services/errors` or `core/errors`) to provide clearer context and allow consistent translation to HTTP responses.",api/services/billing_service.py,316.0,320.0,"if len(cached_values) != len(tenant_ids):
