firefox-ios,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/firefox-ios/pull/6,Incorrect tearDown order in StoriesFeedDiffableDataSourceTests,"The tearDown method calls super.tearDown() before cleaning up test dependencies. In XCTest, super.tearDown() should be called after cleaning up resources to ensure proper cleanup order. Calling super.tearDown() first can cause issues when the parent class attempts to access or clean up resources that are about to be deallocated. The DependencyHelperMock().reset() and collectionView/diffableDataSource cleanup should happen before calling the parent's tearDown to prevent potential crashes or state inconsistencies between tests.",firefox-ios/firefox-ios-tests/Tests/ClientTests/Frontend/StoriesFeed/StoriesFeedDiffableDataSourceTests.swift,28.0,33.0,"    override func tearDown() async throws {
        try await super.tearDown()
        diffableDataSource = nil
        collectionView = nil
        DependencyHelperMock().reset()
    }",
firefox-ios,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/firefox-ios/pull/6,Test state cleanup after super.tearDown in RatingPromptManagerTests,"The tearDown method calls super.tearDown() before cleaning up test-specific state (prefs, subject, userDefaults, etc.). This is problematic because XCTest's tearDown should clean up test-specific resources before calling super.tearDown(). By calling super.tearDown() first, any state or resources that should be cleaned up might leak into subsequent tests or cause undefined behavior. Specifically, calling prefs.clearAll() and subject.reset() after super.tearDown() violates the expected tearDown lifecycle and can lead to test isolation issues where one test's state affects another.",firefox-ios/firefox-ios-tests/Tests/ClientTests/Helpers/RatingPromptManagerTests.swift,36.0,45.0,"    override func tearDown() async throws {
        try await super.tearDown()
        prefs.clearAll()
        subject.reset()
        prefs = nil
        logger = nil
        urlOpenerSpy = nil
        userDefaults = nil
        crashTracker = nil
        subject = nil
    }",
