firefox-ios,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/firefox-ios/pull/9,Inverted reader mode telemetry state tracking,"The recordReaderModeTelemetry function has inverted logic for determining reader mode state. When the reader mode is 'available' (about to be enabled), it reports false instead of true, and for all other states it reports true instead of false. This causes telemetry data to incorrectly track reader mode usage patterns - reporting that reader mode is being disabled when it's actually being enabled and vice versa. This will corrupt analytics data about reader mode feature usage.",firefox-ios/Client/Frontend/Browser/Toolbars/Redux/ToolbarMiddleware.swift,520.0,529.0,"private func recordReaderModeTelemetry(state: AppState, windowUUID: WindowUUID) {
