prefect,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/prefect/pull/4,Regex validation rejects valid uppercase characters in block names,"The `BLOCK_NAME_REGEX` pattern was changed to only accept lowercase letters (`/^[a-z0-9-]+$/`), but the error message still claims to accept both 'lowercase letters, numbers, and dashes'. This creates a functional bug where users cannot create blocks with uppercase letters in the name, even though the validation message suggests they should be able to. This breaks backward compatibility if existing blocks have uppercase names and will confuse users trying to follow naming conventions.",ui-v2/src/components/blocks/block-document-create-dialog/block-document-create-dialog.tsx,41.0,46.0,"const BLOCK_NAME_REGEX = /^[a-z0-9-]+$/;

const BlockNameFormSchema = z.object({
