prefect,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/prefect/pull/13,Removed HTML5 min validation from concurrency limit input,"The concurrency limit input field previously had `min={0}` attribute (HTML5 validation) to prevent negative numbers from being entered. This attribute was removed in this PR change. While the Zod schema still validates that the value must be >= 0, users now lose immediate feedback when trying to enter negative values. They can type a negative number like `-5` and only discover it's invalid after clicking Save, rather than being prevented from entering it in the first place. This degrades the user experience by removing client-side validation that provides instant feedback.",ui-v2/src/components/work-pools/edit/work-pool-edit-form.tsx,106.0,115.0,"<Input
