redis,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/redis/pull/2,Incorrect accumulation of trim job key count across multiple jobs,"The asmActiveTrimStart function uses += instead of = when setting active_trim_current_job_keys, causing the counter to accumulate values across multiple trim jobs instead of being reset for each new job. This leads to incorrect key count reporting in logs and metrics. When multiple trim operations execute sequentially, the counter will show inflated values (sum of all previous jobs plus current job) rather than the accurate count for the current job. This breaks the observability feature added in the PR that logs the number of keys being processed.",src/cluster_asm.c,3306.0,3307.0,"    /* Count the number of keys to trim */
    asmManager->active_trim_current_job_keys = asmCountKeysInSlots(slots);",
redis,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/redis/pull/2,slotRangeArrayIsEqual mutates input arrays causing data corruption,"The slotRangeArrayIsEqual function calls slotRangeArraySortAndMerge on both input parameters, which modifies them in-place by sorting and merging adjacent ranges. This causes critical data corruption when the function is used to compare slot ranges, as it will inadvertently modify the caller's data structures. For example, when asmLookupTaskBySlotRangeArray calls this function at line 579, it corrupts the stored task->slots data. Similarly, at line 1917 in the migrate command handler, calling slotRangeArrayIsEqual(slots, task->slots) will corrupt the existing task's slot range information. This breaks the integrity of stored task data and can lead to incorrect task lookups, corrupted logging output, and unpredictable behavior throughout the ASM system.",,,,"int slotRangeArrayIsEqual(slotRangeArray *slots1, slotRangeArray *slots2) {
    if (slots1->num_ranges != slots2->num_ranges) return 0;

    slotRangeArraySortAndMerge(slots1);
    slotRangeArraySortAndMerge(slots2);

    for (int i = 0; i < slots1->num_ranges; i++) {
        if (slots1->ranges[i].start != slots2->ranges[i].start ||
            slots1->ranges[i].end != slots2->ranges[i].end) {
            return 0;
        }
    }
    return 1;
}",
