redis,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/redis/pull/3,Off-by-one error causing buffer overflow in extractSlotFromKeysResult,"The loop condition in extractSlotFromKeysResult uses `j <= keys_result->numkeys` instead of `j < keys_result->numkeys`, causing an off-by-one error. This results in accessing one element beyond the valid range of both the `keys_result->keys` array and the `slot_buffer` array. When numkeys is N, valid indices are 0 to N-1, but the loop accesses index N, leading to out-of-bounds memory access. This can cause crashes, memory corruption, or unpredictable behavior when processing multi-key commands in cluster mode.",src/cluster.c,1112.0,1123.0,"    /* Allocate temporary buffer for slot tracking */
