redis,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/redis/pull/5,Incorrect memory calculation for QUICKLIST due to wrong denominator,"In the QUICKLIST encoding branch, the average element size calculation uses `elesize/samples` instead of `elesize/elecount`. This divides the accumulated element size by the number of sampled nodes rather than the total element count in those nodes. Since `elecount` represents the sum of all `node->count` values (the actual number of elements), using `samples` (number of nodes) produces an incorrect average that doesn't represent the true per-element memory usage. This causes the MEMORY USAGE command to return wildly inaccurate values for quicklist-encoded lists.",src/object.c,1234.0,1239.0,"            do {
                elesize += sizeof(quicklistNode)+zmalloc_size(node->entry);
                elecount += node->count;
                samples++;
            } while ((node = node->next) && samples < sample_size);
            asize += (double)elesize/samples*ql->count;",
