tauri,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/tauri/pull/8,Inverted mouse button state mapping in tray icon event conversion,"The From implementation for converting tray_icon::MouseButtonState to MouseButtonState has the Up and Down states inverted. When a mouse button is released (Up) from the underlying tray_icon library, it's incorrectly mapped to Down in the Tauri TrayIconEvent, and vice versa. This will cause all tray icon click handlers to receive the opposite button state than what actually occurred, breaking event handling logic that depends on distinguishing between button press and release events. The new_click factory method added in this PR uses MouseButtonState::default() which is Up, but when real events are converted through this From implementation, the states will be backwards.",crates/tauri/src/tray/mod.rs,31.0,37.0,"impl From<tray_icon::MouseButtonState> for MouseButtonState {
  fn from(value: tray_icon::MouseButtonState) -> Self {
    match value {
      tray_icon::MouseButtonState::Up => MouseButtonState::Down,
      tray_icon::MouseButtonState::Down => MouseButtonState::Up,
    }
  }
}",
tauri,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/tauri/pull/8,PatternJavascript struct gated behind isolation feature breaks brownfield pattern,"The PatternJavascript struct was moved behind a #[cfg(feature = ""isolation"")] gate, but this struct is used in webview initialization code (manager/webview.rs line 131) for all pattern types including Pattern::Brownfield. When the isolation feature is disabled, the PatternJavascript struct won't be defined, causing a compilation error in webview.rs when it tries to instantiate PatternJavascript for brownfield applications. This change in the derive attribute placement breaks the fundamental pattern system for non-isolation builds, preventing any Tauri application that doesn't use the isolation pattern from compiling.",crates/tauri/src/pattern.rs,78.0,83.0,"#[cfg(feature = ""isolation"")]
