tauri,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/tauri/pull/12,Wrong field used for UTTypeConformsTo in exported type declarations,"The code incorrectly uses `association.content_types` instead of `exported_type.conforms_to` when populating the `UTTypeConformsTo` array in UTExportedTypeDeclarations. According to Apple's documentation, UTTypeConformsTo should specify the parent types that the exported type inherits from (stored in ExportedFileAssociation.conforms_to), not the content types that the association supports (stored in FileAssociation.content_types). This confusion between two similar-sounding but distinct fields will cause exported file types to declare incorrect type hierarchies, potentially breaking file type recognition and inheritance on macOS.",crates/tauri-bundler/src/bundle/macos/app.rs,284.0,288.0,"          if let Some(content_types) = &association.content_types {
            dict.insert(
              ""UTTypeConformsTo"".into(),
              plist::Value::Array(content_types.iter().map(|s| s.clone().into()).collect()),
            );
          }",
tauri,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/tauri/pull/12,Inverted condition excludes file extensions from CFBundleDocumentTypes,"The condition for adding CFBundleTypeExtensions to CFBundleDocumentTypes is inverted. The code checks `if association.ext.is_empty()` and then attempts to insert the extensions array, which means extensions are only added when the vector is empty (resulting in an empty array being added), and extensions are skipped when they actually exist. This logic error will prevent file associations from being properly registered with their extensions on macOS, causing the system to not recognize which file types the application can handle.",crates/tauri-bundler/src/bundle/macos/app.rs,328.0,338.0,"            if association.ext.is_empty() {
              dict.insert(
                ""CFBundleTypeExtensions"".into(),
                plist::Value::Array(
                  association
                    .ext
                    .iter()
                    .map(|ext| ext.to_string().into())
                    .collect(),
                ),
              );
            }",
tauri,https://github.com/agentic-review-benchmarks/tauri/pull/12,Clippy lint: unnecessary `to_string()` on `&String` when building LSItemContentTypes,"`content_types.iter()` yields `&String`, and calling `to_string()` on a `&String` is typically flagged by clippy as an unnecessary conversion/clone (e.g., `clippy::string_to_string`). With warnings denied, this would fail clippy; use `s.clone()`/`s.to_owned()` instead.",crates/tauri-bundler/src/bundle/macos/app.rs,333.0,336.0,"dict.insert(
